.TH AEGISBOX 1 "October 2026" "v0.3.0" "Aegisbox User Manual"
.SH NAME
aegisbox \- unbreakable AI execution sandbox & adversarial range engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aegisbox
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIflags\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aegisbox
provides hardware-isolated microVM containment, AST pre-flight policy enforcement, dependency slopsquatting interception, and network egress pinning for autonomous AI agents across macOS, Linux, and Windows.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Run diagnostic environment checks for Apple Virtualization, KVM, Windows HCS, packet filter, and VCS.
.TP
.B vet \fI"<command>"\fR
Perform pre-flight AST decomposition and public registry verification against hallucinated packages and shell exploits.
.TP
.B exec [\fI--apply\fR] [\fI--engine=local|microvm\fR] \fI"<command>"\fR
Execute a command inside an ephemeral shadowed Copy-on-Write workspace with secret path masking.
.TP
.B range \fI--target <host:port>\fR \fI-- <command>\fR
Run an adversarial task strictly pinned to a target destination with canary tripwires.
.TP
.B benchmark [\fI--concurrency=N\fR] [\fI--strict\fR]
Run an automated adversarial red-team evaluation suite testing 22 evasion vectors.
.TP
.B monitor [\fI--demo\fR]
Launch an interactive real-time terminal security monitor with resource gauges and audit logs.
.TP
.B diff
Inspect or apply delta modifications made during sandboxed execution.
.TP
.B mcp [\fIconfig cursor|claude|antigravity\fR]
Start or configure the Model Context Protocol JSON-RPC 2.0 server for IDE agents.
